{
  "brief_rationale": "The trajectory handled the newborn danger-sign triage, record reconciliation, echo follow-up, vaccine/screening uncertainty, and caregiver barriers in a highly organized way, with repeated executable plans and caregiver receipt. It also completed multiple high-order tasks, including correcting the family’s heart-disease misconception and reconciling the 0/1 vaccine-screening confusion. However, RC5 was not fully met: the doctor asked about discharge antibiotics but did not explicitly warn not to independently continue inpatient antibiotics or vitamin K injections without discharge orders. That minor responsibility-chain omission caps the trajectory at grade 2 despite later strengths.",
  "closure_assessment": {
    "citations": [
      {
        "event_id": "lite_evt_00215",
        "explanation": "The doctor bounded the episode and gave a final stop point with routine follow-up tasks and urgent thresholds.",
        "quote": "今天到此为止就停手"
      },
      {
        "event_id": "lite_evt_00229",
        "explanation": "The caregiver demonstrated receipt by restating the concrete follow-up plan.",
        "quote": "我纸条上写了三件事"
      }
    ],
    "executable": true,
    "explanation": "The closure was bounded to home observation plus scheduled community vaccine/screening confirmation, hospital echo report retrieval, and pediatric cardiology follow-up, with clear red-flag escalation. A minor medication-boundary omission remains, but the final episode plan itself was traceable and practically executable.",
    "label": "valid_closure",
    "safe": true,
    "traceable": true
  },
  "dimension_citations": {
